      "summary": "The adapter’s walk handler also processes arrow keys used to navigate the rack menu, which can move the avatar before route confirmation.",
      "findingList": [
        {
          "severity": "major",
          "file": "frontend/src/hangar/GuideLineAdapter.tsx",
          "line": 73,
          "message": "Limit walk-step handling to the walk region. Arrow navigation in the rack menu currently bubbles to the adapter’s section handler and moves the avatar.",
          "confidence": 0.86,
          "category": "logic-error",
          "evidence": {
            "codePathTraced": "When entries are present, the adapter attaches its walk key handler to the section containing HangarRackMenu. Arrow key events from rack-menu items bubble to that section, where the handler treats them as walk steps.",
            "failureScenario": "When a user presses ArrowDown to navigate the open rack menu, the event can also move the avatar and recompute the guide route before the user confirms an entry."
